🔥 Complete Commented Code (Clean + Correct)
class Solution {
    public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
        int n = prices.length;

        // dp[idx][turn]
        // idx → current day
        // turn → 0 = BUY allowed, 1 = SELL allowed
        int dp[][] = new int[n][2];

        // initialize with -1
        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++){
            Arrays.fill(dp[i], -1);
        }

        return help(prices, 0, 0, dp);
    }

    public int help(int[] prices, int idx, int turn, int dp[][]){

        // Base case: no days left
        if(idx >= prices.length) return 0;

        // Already computed
        if(dp[idx][turn] != -1) return dp[idx][turn];

        int profit = 0;

        // BUY allowed
        if(turn == 0){
            int buy = -prices[idx] + help(prices, idx+1, 1, dp);
            int skip = help(prices, idx+1, 0, dp);

            profit = Math.max(buy, skip);
        }
        else{
            // SELL allowed
            int sell = prices[idx] + help(prices, idx+2, 0, dp); // cooldown
            int skip = help(prices, idx+1, 1, dp);

            profit = Math.max(sell, skip);
        }

        return dp[idx][turn] = profit;
    }
}
🎮 Intuition (Game Visualization)
State	Meaning
turn = 0	You don’t have stock → can BUY
turn = 1	You have stock → can SELL
🔥 Why idx + 2 ?

👉 After selling:

Day i → SELL
Day i+1 → cooldown (no action)
Next possible → i+2
🧠 Profit Logic (VERY IMPORTANT)
Buy = -price
Sell = +price

👉 So automatically:

profit = sell - buy
📌 REVISION NOTES
Problem = Cooldown stock problem
DP = 2D → (idx, turn)
No need of k
Sell → jump idx + 2
Buy → go to idx + 1
DP stores future max profit
⚡ Quick Click Points
State: (idx, buy/sell)
Cooldown handled by idx+2
Time: O(n * 2)
Space: O(n * 2)
Memoization avoids recomputation
⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Using idx+1 after sell
❌ Forgetting cooldown
❌ Using k (not needed here)
❌ Thinking subtraction needed

🎤 Interview Counter Questions
1. Why no k here?

👉 Because transactions are unlimited (only cooldown constraint)

2. Why idx + 2 after sell?

👉 Due to cooldown (1 day rest)

3. Can we solve without DP?

👉 Yes, using greedy + states (but DP is safer)

4. Can we optimize space?

👉 Yes → only 3 variables needed

5. What if no cooldown?

👉 Then it becomes simple unlimited transactions problem

